# Analytics — one stack per surface (mandatory)

Portal session UI lives in **`streamclone-pulse/packages/analytics-console`** (linked into `streampulse-web`). Hub UI lives in **`streampulse-web/src/ui/components/hub/`**. Extension charts live in **`streamclone-pulse/src/ui/`**.

## Before finishing any analytics portal task

1. Run `npm run check:analytics-overlap` from `streampulse-web/` (must pass).
2. Run `npm install` in `streampulse-web/` if you edited `packages/analytics-console` or `packages/pulse-charts`.
3. Hard-refresh `http://127.0.0.1:5173` after restart — HMR does not reload linked packages reliably.

## DELETE or GATE — never stack

| Surface | Single owner | Never mount together |
|---------|--------------|----------------------|
| Session Moments tab | `SessionRecapMomentsStrip` **or** `MomentReviewPanel` | Both in same tab without `recapMomentsAvailable` ternary |
| Live channel URL | Redirect to canonical session slug | Bare `/analytics/:login` chart + separate session page |
| VOD fallback | `resolveSessionFallbackVodId` (current session only) | `for (const row of sidebarStreams)` VOD scan |
| Hub chart | `HubActivityChart` | `GlobalActivityChart`, second hub chart |
| Session chart legend | `AnalyticsChart` toolbar | Duplicate legend inside `PulseMultiSignalChart` |
| Session chart viewport controls | `AnalyticsChart` range row (`data-chart-range-row`) | `[data-chart-viewport-controls]` floated over the plot inside `PulseMultiSignalChart` |
| Selected-moment detail | `SelectedMomentCompactCard` in the Moments rail | `SelectedMomentPanel` below the chart, a "top moment" button in `StreamRecapPanel` |
| Moment row markup | `MomentRow` | Bespoke rows inside `SessionRecapMomentsStrip` / `MomentReviewPanel` |
| Console motion CSS | `analytics-chart-motion.css` (console surfaces) **and** `pulse-chart-motion.css` (chart primitives), disjoint | The same selector or `@keyframes` declared in both — the portal loads both, so one silently wins |

## Adding a feature

- **Replace** the old component mount, **or** add an explicit `if/else` gate documented in code.
- **Delete** unwired routes/components in the same PR (e.g. duplicate date page, dead chart file).
- **Update** `tests/recapMomentsAvailable.test.ts` or overlap guard if the gate pattern changes.

`npm run check:analytics-overlap` and `pages:deploy:prod` **fail the build** if these regressions return.
